WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.380
I love close-ups in IMAX because

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.980
the expressions of the actors

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.680
and the nuance just comes out better in IMAX.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.880
Joaquin and I spend a ton of time together

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.560
just talking about Arthur and Joker

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.200
and where the laugh comes from

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.740
and what Arthur looks like

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.020
and how Arthur walks and talks

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.400
and obviously things you talk about with actors

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.720
in general.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.100
But with Joaquin,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.900
it always seems to go a little bit deeper.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.260
I've never really met an actor like Joaquin.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.940
He made the process uniquely thrilling.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.820
[Laughter]

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.300
[Music]

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.360
You're not immune sitting at the desk

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.760
you're in it.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.760
and you feel the character

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.120
you feel the emotion

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.960
and you feel what he's doing.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.400
I used to think that

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.400
my life was a tragedy

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.400
but now I realize

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.140
it's a comedy.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.140
As the dialogue mixer,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.140
there's a lot that I will do

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.140
from a mixing standpoint

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:14.680
to push some of the intimacy moments

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.700
with him and things where I can actually

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.900
make it feel like you are closer to him

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.160
maybe closer to him than you want to be

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.880
at times.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.620
I love the way the Gotham looks

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.560
in this movie.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.100
The sirens sound different

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.520
they don't sound like New York sirens

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.380
and that was another tall order

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.380
that Todd wanted.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.800
We weren't supposed to make

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.060
Hill Street Blues quote unquote

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.120
we were supposed to make Gotham.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.740
The character of Arthur is a slow burn

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.680
turning into Joker

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.640
so part of the magic of Joaquin

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.920
is that ability to kind of tweak the performance

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.840
so that transformation happens so slowly.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.680
We had to sonically take the ride with Arthur

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.800
from where you saw him

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.260
to where he ends up.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.560
Playing with that was a lot of fun

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.260
but it's a very delicate tricky thing.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.680
As he transforms

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.340
the lighting gets a bit darker

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.900
camera gets a bit lower

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.900
he becomes a bit more grand.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.880
I've been fortunate enough to six movies with Todd.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.780
On this movie

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.200
more than any we've ever done before

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.940
we would just constantly remind ourselves

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.520
there's no compromise here.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.340
This has to be the best thing we've ever done.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.420
You know, pressure makes diamonds.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.360
It is unlike any other DC movie

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.360
you have ever seen.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.460
I think that a lot of people

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.180
are gonna be surprised by Joker.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.200
You're gonna walk away questioning some things.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.320
It's a good ride

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.200
that's for sure.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.600
Seeing it in IMAX is just gonna heighten

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.460
that experience.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.860
It's just the experience you can't get

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.500
anywhere else.

